{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy to data/models.json (gitignored) and edit, then point",
    "CUSTOM_MODEL_LIST_PATH at it. Under ./data because that is what compose",
    "mounts into the container; a path elsewhere resolves on the host only.",
    "Every model carries its own endpoint and its own key, so one scan can reach",
    "several providers at once. Keys are read from this file and never stored in",
    "the database, written to a result, or sent anywhere but the endpoint beside them.",
    "",
    "model_id    what the provider calls the model. Goes in the request body, names",
    "            the engine on the command line, and is stored on every result row.",
    "model_title display only, for the picker in the UI. Safe to rename at any time.",
    "api_key     the key for THIS endpoint.",
    "v1_endpoint the OpenAI-compatible base URL. '/v1' is appended if you leave it off.",
    "",
    "A scan needs three kinds of model reachable: the engine under test, the judge",
    "(JUDGE_MODEL in .env), and at least one back-translator from the panel. The",
    "tool checks all three before spending anything and names whatever is missing."
  ],
  "models": [
    {
      "model_title": "GPT-4o",
      "model_id": "gpt-4o",
      "api_key": "sk-your-openai-key",
      "v1_endpoint": "https://api.openai.com/v1"
    },
    {
      "model_title": "GPT-4o mini (judge)",
      "model_id": "gpt-4o-mini",
      "api_key": "sk-your-openai-key",
      "v1_endpoint": "https://api.openai.com/v1"
    },
    {
      "model_title": "DeepSeek Chat",
      "model_id": "deepseek-chat",
      "api_key": "sk-your-deepseek-key",
      "v1_endpoint": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1"
    },
    {
      "model_title": "Qwen2.5 72B (local vLLM)",
      "model_id": "Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct",
      "api_key": "not-needed",
      "v1_endpoint": "http://localhost:8001/v1"
    }
  ]
}
